  "ref": "MRK.10.34",
  "review_notes": [
    "Two units changed. s005 ἐμπτύσουσιν now takes 'shall spit upon' headed on 'spit'; s006 αὐτῷ now takes a bare 'him'. Everything else is as the verse pass returned it.",
    "The competing reading — 'upon' as a rule 21 case helper on the dative pronoun — is what the verse originally had, and it remains defensible in isolation. What defeats it is the chapter: ἐμβλέπω governs a dative at 10:21 and 10:27 in the identical English shape and keeps 'upon' with the verb, and no source difference distinguishes the two.",
    "This does not disturb the genuine case helpers at 10:17 ('to him' after γονυπετήσας) or 10:35 ('of thee' after αἰτήσωμεν): neither verb carries a prepositional prefix for the English word to answer to."
  ]
